    {
      "slug": "claude-sdk-rs-not-on-disk",
      "scope": {
        "repo": "engine-rs"
      },
      "kind": "known_issue",
      "text": "EN.2.A's native transport (claude-sdk-rs execute_claude + Config, post repair-pass) is NOT buildable/verifiable from engine-rs: the claude-sdk-rs repo is not on disk at ../../../claude-sdk-rs and its repair-pass state is unconfirmed. Per the master-plan block, if the repair pass hasn't landed, fall back to the tmux/file-drop 'bastion ask' seam (parity with orchestrator/app/services/claude_code/bastion_backend.py:128). The user wants to first review a Claude Code Rust SDK on GitHub and compare it against claude-sdk-rs before the transport is decided, so transport primacy is deliberately deferred.",
      "clears_when": "the ClaudeCodeStep transport is decided and its decision file (D4) is written",
      "created": "2026-07-03"
